# FINAL ACCEPTANCE TEST

The work is NOT complete until the following scenario succeeds without manual code changes:

1. Create a new tenant from the Platform Admin.
2. Configure branding (logo, colors, fonts, metadata).
3. Select a storefront template (e.g., the AMOOKSCO V2 theme).
4. Publish the tenant.
5. Access the tenant via `/store/{slug}`, subdomain, and custom domain.
6. Confirm the tenant website, tenant portal, customer experience, and platform admin are all visually and functionally isolated, with no AfruHeritage branding leaking into tenant-facing pages.
7. Run a full build, automated regression tests, and end-to-end validation. All checks must pass before the work is considered complete.

**Do not stop at "build passes."** The objective is a production-ready, reusable multi-tenant SaaS where adding a new customer requires configuration—not source code changes.
